SHA256: 40530266ef9aeb482ad15dca32f28d504b60634e8abbd1bda22047865dd9a681
Section: libs
Priority: optional
Description: Qualcomm FastRPC userspace for the OnePlus Pad 3 (erhai): CDSP transport
 This is the SHARED FastRPC layer of erhai: the Qualcomm userspace built from
 github.com/qualcomm/fastrpc, plus the DSP-side payload trees a FastRPC client
 uploads to the DSP. It is what makes /dev/fastrpc-cdsp usable at all, so the
 NPU/HTP stack (oneplus-erhai-npu) and any other FastRPC client need it.
 .
  - client libraries in /usr/local/lib: libcdsprpc (SONAME libcdsprpc.so.1),
    libadsprpc, libsdsprpc and the three *_default_listener shims;
  - cdsprpcd, the remotefs daemon for the COMPUTE DSP (the Linux equivalent of
    Android's `cdsprpcd rootpd cdsp`), with a hardened unit
    (cdsprpcd.service: ConditionPathExists-gated so a kernel without the CDSP
    SKIPS it) and a drop-in setting ADSP_LIBRARY_PATH/DSP_LIBRARY_PATH to the
    DSP payload trees;
  - the `fastrpc` group (usr/lib/sysusers.d/fastrpc.conf) and the udev rule that
    hands /dev/fastrpc-* to it (root:fastrpc 0640) and ACLs /dev/dma_heap/system
    -- uaccess cannot be used here, the FastRPC nodes are misc devices;
    the postinst also puts the desktop accounts into the group, which needs a
    re-login to take effect;
  - /etc/environment.d/57-erhai-fastrpc-unsigned.conf (FASTRPC_UNSIGNED_PD=1):
    the Linux QNN/ggml DSP skels are unsigned-only, and QNN picks
    signed-vs-unsigned from the platform info, so the CDSP refuses the PD image
    (0x8000054f) without it;
  - the DSP payload trees clients read from: /usr/lib/rfsa/adsp,
    /usr/lib/rfsa/cdsp and /usr/share/qcom/hexagon/v79 (fastrpc_shell_3 +
    _unsigned_3, the Hexagon C++ runtime, the QNN HTP v79 skel, the HTP runtime
    and the ggml-htp skels, from OxygenOS 16.0.9.400, the public QNN/QAIRT
    releases and Qualcomm's PyPI GenieX tooling);
  - fastrpc_test + fastrpc-healthcheck (bring-up/diagnostic tools).
 .
 DELIBERATELY NOT SHIPPED: the adsprpcd/sdsprpcd/gdsprpcd daemons and their
 units -- the ADSP/SDSP paths on erhai are served by oneplus-erhai-sensors'
 hexagonrpcd-erhai -- the libtool .la files, and the manual backup copies of the
 QNN skel (*.previous, *.qai_appbuilder) that nothing loads.
 .
 Kernel side (NO kernel package is recommended or suggested on purpose: the
 erhai kernel is mandatory for Ubuntu on this tablet and ships in the image):
 the CDSP remoteproc must be enabled (oneplus-erhai-linux from the 7.2 +b63
 build on, or any 7.3-rc* line) and the firmware must carry the cdsp split image
 (oneplus-erhai-firmware >= 1.2).

