Description: Patched llama.cpp for the OnePlus Pad 3 (erhai): CPU + Adreno OpenCL + Hexagon NPU
 llama.cpp (ggml 0.24.0, upstream 6f41ac5) built with the local erhai patch
 set, installed under /opt/llama.cpp so it never shadows a distro build.
 .
 The patches are the price of running ggml on this device:
  - OpenCL/Adreno (rusticl): accept the OpenCL 3.0 subgroup family instead of
    the legacy cl_khr_subgroups name, empty REQD_SUBGROUP_SIZE_* for a compiler
    that lacks cl_qcom_reqd_sub_group_size, keep the qcom shuffle mapping in
    mul_mv_f16_f32_l4.cl conditional, portable float32 in the nine
    gemm_moe_*_ns.cl kernels, and is_qualcomm_adreno_compiler() so the
    unparsable Mesa driver version stops skipping the 1d_8x_flat decode
    kernels the dispatch path still uses (without it every single-token decode
    died with clSetKernelArg error -48);
  - a hexagon backend loader fix: ggml-backend-reg.cpp also accepts the legacy
    ggml_backend_<name>_reg() entry point, which is what the prebuilt Hexagon
    backend exports;
  - --offload-spec / -os (env LLAMA_ARG_OFFLOAD_SPEC): explicit device
    placement ('HTP0:8', 'HTP0:layers=0-3,GPUOpenCL:layers=4-5,CPU:rest',
    'HTP0:bytes=2G'), rules left to right, first match wins, unnamed layers
    stay on the CPU.
 .
 The vendor Hexagon (HTP) backend that this build loads for NPU offload,
 libggml-hexagon.so + libggml-htp-v79.so, is shipped under
 /opt/llama.cpp/share/hexagon-v79/ (Qualcomm's public GenieX/qai_appbuilder
 binaries -- DSP-side blobs, not built here).
 .
 llama-erhai and llama-erhai-server wrap the binaries with the environment the
 device stack needs and REFUSE to run on the GPU by default: an Adreno OpenCL
 fault on this pad takes the panel down with it (2026-09-22: ggml-opencl
 GGML_ASSERT -> msm hangcheck -> drm recover loop -> hard reset).  The safe
 local-LLM devices are the CPU and the Hexagon NPU.
 .
 NOTE the NPU route additionally needs the CDSP userspace stack (cdsprpcd,
 libcdsprpc, /usr/lib/rfsa, the fastrpc group) -- see the README shipped in
 /usr/share/doc/oneplus-erhai-llamacpp/.

