Section: utils
Priority: optional
Description: Hexagon NPU / compute-DSP (CDSP) workload layer for the OnePlus Pad 3 (erhai)
 The NPU/HTP half of erhai's Hexagon stack: the file tree the CDSP is served,
 the health report and the user front end.  The TRANSPORT layer (libcdsprpc,
 cdsprpcd, the fastrpc group, the udev rule, the DSP payload trees) is
 oneplus-erhai-fastrpc, which this package depends on; the ADSP path stays in
 oneplus-erhai-sensors.
  - the complete CDSP FastRPC remote-filesystem tree served to the DSP
    (/var/lib/hexagonfs-cdsp/dsp/cdsp): fastrpc_shell_3 +
    fastrpc_shell_unsigned_3 (the user-PD shells), the Hexagon CoProcessor
    (HTP) runtime libs from the device's own dsp partition, the vendor QNN
    HTP v79 skel (libQnnHtpV79Skel.so) and the C++ runtime the skels link
    against -- all taken from OxygenOS 16.0.9.400;
  - hexagonrpcd-cdsp.service: the DISABLED fallback daemon (our hexagonrpcd
    fork, attaching to /dev/fastrpc-cdsp as the DSP's root PD).  The daemon that
    works with this firmware is Qualcomm's cdsprpcd from oneplus-erhai-fastrpc;
    the fallback stays for a kernel/firmware combination whose apps_std ABI is
    the one the upstream RPC host expects;
  - erhai-npu-status.sh: one-shot health report of the whole chain (kernel
    DT/firmware, remoteproc, FastRPC nodes, transport, daemon, payload), with an
    optional --pd-test proving the DSP executes a host-uploaded shell;
  - npu-llm: an ollama-style front end (pull/run/chat/list/rm/doctor/models)
    running GGUF models on the NPU through the GenieX SDK's llama.cpp backend,
    hiding the two local quirks (the fastrpc group and the CDSP mapping space);
  - erhai-cdsp-restart.sh: recovery for an exhausted FastRPC mapping arena
    (restarts the CDSP remoteproc only -- NEVER the ADSP, that freezes the SoC).
 .
 Kernel side (NO dependency declared on purpose: the erhai kernel is mandatory
 for Ubuntu on this tablet and ships in the image): the CDSP remoteproc must be
 enabled, i.e. oneplus-erhai-linux from the 7.2 +b63 build on, or any 7.3-rc*
 line, booting the OxygenOS cdsp.mdt/cdsp_dtb.mdt split image with the
 OEM-identical carveouts (0x9d200000+0x1900000, 0x9eb00000+0x80000), plus
 oneplus-erhai-firmware >= 1.2.
 .
 NOTE: the QNN *host* runtime (libQnnHtp.so / libQnnHtpV79Stub.so) is not
 shippable -- Qualcomm distributes it for Android (bionic) and through the
 account-gated QNN/Hexagon SDK.  The DSP side is complete here, and npu-llm
 reaches the NPU through the GenieX SDK's own host runtime (pip install --user
 geniex, which also fetches its SDK zip).

