Section: games
Priority: optional
Description: Steam (native arm64 client) for aarch64 Linux
 Valve's native 64-bit ARM Steam client, packaged so that a plain
 "apt install steam" gives a working client on an arm64 machine.
 .
 The package is deliberately small: it ships Valve's BOOTSTRAP only
 (steamrtarm64/steam, ~10 MB) under /usr/lib/steam, and the client downloads
 the rest of itself from Valve's CDN on the first start.  Measured on a bare
 bootstrap (2026-10-17): 654 MB downloaded, 3.1 GB on disk, including the
 steamrt3c container runtime the client now runs inside.
 .
 /usr/lib/steam is NOT the directory the client runs from.  Steam's root must
 be writable by the account running it -- the client updates itself and writes
 its config, caches and logs inside its own tree -- which a dpkg-owned package
 tree cannot allow, so /usr/bin/steam seeds the bootstrap into the user's own
 writable Steam root (~/.local/share/Steam, Valve's default) and starts it
 there.  Existing files in that root are never overwritten or deleted, so the
 client's own updates always win.
 .
 No account data is shipped: no login record, no remembered-credentials cache,
 no configuration, no library, no cache -- a freshly installed client starts at
 the sign-in prompt and asks for the user's own Steam credentials.
 .
